a Connecticut man charged with killing a  hotel worker in the Caribbean is  scheduled to appear in court this  morning  Scott Hapgood arrived back on the island  of Anguilla yesterday he's charged in  the death of Kenny Mitchell in April  Errol Barnett reports from Anguilla on  what can we expect at today's hearing  for second time this week Scott Hapgood  returned to Anguilla Wednesday with  security by his side local radio host DJ  hammer says the case has upset many on  the island the persons believe that mr.  Hapgood  was treated especially outraged has  escalated to threats against a 44  year-old and his family on Tuesday  hapgoods attorney blasted the decision  requiring her client to appear in person  it is cruel and unreasonable justice to  drag someone into the jurisdiction to  put them in harm's way on April 13th  Hapgood claims Mitchell an employee of  this luxury resort showed up at his  family's room with a knife demanding  money during a violent struggle Hopkins  family says he was bitten and stabbed  Mitchell who was beaten and suffocated  died shortly after a toxicology report  showing Mitchell had alcohol and cocaine  in his system no one close to Mitchell  living on the island agreed to appear on  camera CBS News has contacted a lawyer  representing Mitchell but has not heard  back Hapgood spoke exclusively with CBS  News on Monday I know that all I did was  defend my young daughters in front of an  attacker that was crazed and desperate  Errol Barnett for CBS this morning in  the capital of the British Caribbean  territory of Anguilla
 

